WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.975
This can be interesting.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.944
A door not gone terribly wrong.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:11.644
Tonight, new details

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.712
in the case of a man accused

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.847
of shooting a 16 year old

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.849
who mistakenly rang his doorbell.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.051
Let's just get right into this, Chad,

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.052
right off the bat.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:22.255
Tell me how big of a

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.256
part of your job

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.658
actually is knocking on people's doors?

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.927
If I was to put it in percentage wise,

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.196
I would say about between 20 and 30%.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.732
A lot of realtors choose not to do it

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.567
because of situations.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.170
And as soon as I knock on a door,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.006
I always step off the porch

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.243
or try to give at least six feet

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.278
between the doorstep and myself.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:46.513
No, it's interesting hearing you do that.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:47.947
We do the exact same thing.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.115
And really the key for me

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.117
is I want to be able to look to my left

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.018
and look to my right

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:52.519
and see that

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.055
I have space to potentially jump out of

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.656
the way if somebody comes out

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:58.958
with a gun.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.593
I try to be as loud as I can.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.163
Like a delivery. Good morning, you know.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.130
Good afternoon.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:04.798
Good evening.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:07.167
Delivery from the bottom of the stairs.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.002
Like, I try to, like, attract

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.770
attention to myself

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.204
in a way

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.239
that's, like, disarming in my mind.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:13.506
Yeah.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.874
You're just trying to let them know

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:15.909
that if you see someone

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:16.876
walking up in the next

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.145
few seconds, I come in peace.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:19.813
I'm a I'm

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.848
a bike messenger in San Francisco.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.683
I was accosted by somebody

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.285
in a nice neighborhood.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.853
Nice neighborhood.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.221
I wanted gamification.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:28.755
Who are you?

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:31.224
Who are you?

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:31.825
Why do I.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:32.826
Why do you think that?

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.694
I have to answer questions?

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:35.929
Don't think I don't know why

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.098
you came over here and stop me.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.132
Because you think I belong

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.567
in another neighborhood, right?

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.034
At first,

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:41.901
he is going to call the cops

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:42.335
because he thought

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.070
I was stealing packages.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.138
And then after I, you know,

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.140
I pressed him back a little bit.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.609
He he said that I was being threatening

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:50.710
and that I was scared.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.478
You know,

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.178
a lot of these people say

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.179
they do feel unsafe

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.547
and they do feel like

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.282
they perceive somebody as a threat.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.851
But if you perceive somebody as a threat,

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.119
why not just call the police?

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.019
Why not let them?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:00.887
I mean, that's what we pay them

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:01.454
for, right?

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.722
If I don't know

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.090
too much about the neighborhood,

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.992
I probably won't go

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.627
there and introduce myself.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.628
I have the luxury

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.196
of picking and choosing.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.631
Unfortunately, these gentlemen

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.299
do not do Ontario.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.400
All of this makes me think

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.768
of a little bit of your situation,

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:16.803
and I know you can't talk

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.537
too much about it,

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.606
but you've been actually shot

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:22.308
at on the job. Yes, sir.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.577
I always feel like my press ID.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.379
